.TH "VTTREGION.VIEWPORTANCHORX" "3JS" "June 18, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
VTTRegion.viewportAnchorX \- VTTRegion: viewportAnchorX property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]viewportAnchorX\f[B]\f[R] property of the
\f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] interface represents the x\-coordinate of the
viewport anchor, as a percentage of the video\(cqs width.
.SH VALUE
A number, in the range \f[CR]0\f[R] to \f[CR]100\f[R] inclusive,
representing the x\-coordinate of the viewport anchor as a percentage of
the video\(cqs width.
The default is \f[CR]0\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]IndexSizeError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown when set to a value that is negative or greater than
\f[CR]100\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
In the following example, a new \f[CR]VTTRegion\f[R] is created, then
the value of \f[CR]viewportAnchorX\f[R] is set to \f[CR]25\f[R].
The value is then printed to the console.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] region = \f[B]new\f[R] VTTRegion();
region.viewportAnchorX = 25; \f[I]// Place the region 25% from the left edge of the video\f[R]
console.log(region.viewportAnchorX);
.EE
